translation.securityRedTeaming.report.target	Target
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.testingPeriod	Testing period
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.generated	Report generated
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.findings	Findings
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.executiveSummary	Executive summary
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.executiveSummaryBody_one	Devin performed an authorized penetration test of {{domain}}. The engagement identified {{count}} finding in scope: {{critical}} critical, {{high}} high, {{medium}} medium and {{low}} low. The finding below includes the evidence Devin collected and a recommended remediation.
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.executiveSummaryBody_other	Devin performed an authorized penetration test of {{domain}}. The engagement identified {{count}} findings in scope: {{critical}} critical, {{high}} high, {{medium}} medium and {{low}} low. Each finding below includes the evidence Devin collected and a recommended remediation.
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.executiveSummaryBody_zero	Devin performed an authorized penetration test of {{domain}}. The engagement identified no findings in scope.
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.scope	Scope and authorization
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.scopeDomain	Target domain
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.scopeHosts	Additional in-scope hosts
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.scopeNoHosts	None. Testing was limited to the target domain.
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.scopeRepos	Source repositories
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.scopeNoRepos	None. Testing ran against the live target without source code.
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.scopeAuthorization	Authorization
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.scopeAuthorizationBody	The target owner authorized this test, and Cognition verified ownership of the target domain before testing began. Testing traffic was restricted to the hosts listed above.
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.methodology	Methodology
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.methodologyReconnaissance	Reconnaissance: Devin mapped the target's reachable endpoints, technologies and authentication flows, using the source repositories to guide coverage.
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.methodologyReconnaissanceNoRepos	Reconnaissance: Devin mapped the target's reachable endpoints, technologies and authentication flows by probing the live target, without access to source code.
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.methodologyBody	Testing: Devin exercised the application as an external attacker and as each provided user role, covering authentication and session handling, access control, injection, server-side request forgery, business logic and sensitive data exposure, aligned with the OWASP Web Security Testing Guide.\
Validation: each candidate issue was reproduced against the live target before it was reported. Unconfirmed issues were dismissed and are not included.\
Reporting: findings are rated by impact and exploitability. Secrets observed during testing are redacted.
translation.securityRedTeaming.report.findingsSummary	Findings summary
